{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>I shall see him.</b> What this people will do to your people." "<b>Step forth from Jacob.</b> Corporeal and eternal, as it says: וּמַצְדִּיקֵי הָרַבִּים כַּכּוֹכָבִים לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד (Daniel 12:3)." "<b>And smite the borders of Moab.</b> Even though all the nations will perish from the breath of Elohim, as it says: כִּי אֶעֱשֶׂה כָלָה בְּכָל הַגּוֹיִם (Jeremiah 30:11) — behold, upon Edom and Moab His vengeance will be at the hand of Israel, these two nations having been His enemies forever and the plotters of His harm (Sanhedrin, chapter Ḥelek)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {2 "Sforno reads the verse's 'star out of Jacob' as referring to the people of Israel; the lemma translated 'Step forth from Jacob' renders דרך כוכב, which he interprets as Israel's enduring corporeal-national existence, not a individual messianic figure."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:05.063223614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}